  clipName: BackWallLean
  author: 
  rigVersion: SubwayCarry-Dummy-01
  rigSignature: 415899A36E5F36473438AE1BC4FE6EC914F96F9E5C882A7651388F4C7C395EF5
  description: Back-wall lean authored at 60 fps with pose keys every 30 frames.
    Stand quietly, incline the whole body from the ankles approximately four degrees
    so only the upper scapular back contacts the rear wall. Keep the feet grounded,
    knees nearly straight, arms relaxed, and gaze level. Both feet are 14.35 cm nearer
    the fixed rear wall than the original version. The left toes remain level on
    the floor during heel lift. The optional posture shift moves the pelvis backward,
    brings the buttocks and lower/middle back close to the wall, gently rolls the
    upper back forward off the wall, keeps the right leg almost straight, and moves
    the left forefoot 12 cm backward with a 16-degree heel lift and a softly flexed
    left knee. Reverse the change smoothly. Exact matching first/last poses permit
    seamless repetition.
  sourceRig: {fileID: 1648686333044378150, guid: 9d1a15a96145a924e838aae19388632a, type: 3}
